# Simulator build products and results. Evidence is published by the CI job
# that produced it, not committed from a working copy: a results file in the
# repository has no configuration attached to it and cannot be told from one
# produced by a different build.
sim_build/
results/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/

# Generated vendor IP. The RTL is marked "Actel Proprietary and Confidential"
# and is redistributable only under the Microchip licence, so it is generated
# rather than stored. `make ip` produces it.
#
# The `*.lock.json` files are NOT ignored, and that is the point: a digest of the IP
# is not the IP. Committing it lets two engineers who generate independently
# prove they got the same core, and lets a reviewer see which core the
# evidence was produced against, without the repository carrying vendor RTL.
ip/*/

# Generated simulation wrappers live under sim_build/ and are already ignored
# with it. Listed here so nobody adds one deliberately: a wrapper restates a
# block's ports, and a stored copy describes a block that has gained or lost a
# port the moment one changes.
**/tb_top.sv

# The coverage page. Generated from items, tests and results; a committed copy
# is a second answer to the same question and goes stale the moment a test is
# written. CI publishes it as an artifact.
public/

# Raw Verilator coverage data, one file per test module and several megabytes
# each. Measurement output, not a source: regenerate with FSVERIF_COVERAGE=1.
coverage/
